{"name":"Bigfoot","hex":"#715145","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Bigfoot","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A very large, hairy, humanoid creature, similar to the yeti, said to live in the wilderness areas of the United States and Canada, especially the Pacific Northwest."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An individual creature of this type."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Bigfoot"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bigfoot","blocks":[{"text":"Bigfoot, or Sasquatch, is a large, hairy, mythical humanoid creature said to inhabit forests in North America, particularly in the Pacific Northwest. Bigfoot is featured in both American and Canadian folklore, and since the mid-20th century has become a cultural icon, permeating popular culture and becoming the subject of its own distinct subculture."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Patterson_Gimlin_Bigfoot.jpg/330px-Patterson_Gimlin_Bigfoot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bigfoot","wikidata":"Q44810"},{"title":"Bigfoot (truck)","blocks":[{"text":"Bigfoot is the name of a series of monster trucks, originally built and owned by American off-road racing enthusiast and auto shop owner Bob Chandler."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Bigfoot_12-5-09_Eureka_Walmart_032.jpg/330px-Bigfoot_12-5-09_Eureka_Walmart_032.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bigfoot_(truck)","wikidata":"Q4906841"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/2016ShawneeBigfoot.jpg/500px-2016ShawneeBigfoot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/2016ShawneeBigfoot.jpg/1280px-2016ShawneeBigfoot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnai